> Module Filers

> Using Types
> Using Standard_deduction as SD

# Filers: age, marital status, residency, dependency of the filers

Direct File module `filers.xml` ("DF" below,
`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/filers.xml`, 5,544
lines) plus the spouse facts in `filers.xml` lines 3270 to 4480. Issue #15,
scope.md section 5.1. Tests are in `catala/tests/test_filers.catala_en`; the
oracle comparison is `difftest/mappings/filers.mjs`.

Not modelled here, on purpose (issue #15 "Out of scope", CONVENTIONS section 2):
names, TIN and SSN validity, identity PINs, address, phone, e-mail, MeF and PDF
helper facts (`...Xml`, `...Indicator`, `mefFullName`, ...), the state-scoping
facts (`/flowKnockoutUnsupportedState`, `/hasIncomeInScope`, the W-2 and
1099-INT state options; owner #36), the per-filer student and disabled flags
and the Credit for the Elderly or Disabled helpers (owner #30), the Saver's
Credit and CDCC per-filer facts (owners #29, #28), and `/MFSSpouseFilingReturn`
(deprecated in DF; the spec uses `/MFSSpouseFilingReturnDerived`).

The inputs are complete (`catala/CONVENTIONS.md` section 3). A DF `Writable`
fact that the questionnaire only asks under some condition (for example
`/spouseLivedTogetherMonths`, asked only if the spouses did not live together
all year) is still an input here; its value is read only where DF reads it.
The filing status is an input (CONVENTIONS section 7), so `treat_as_mfj` and
the facts that depend on it need no second pass.

Two filers at most. `primary_filer` is the filer with `isPrimaryFiler`,
`secondary_filer` the other one (DF `/primaryFiler`, `/secondaryFiler`). For a
return that is not joint the secondary entry carries whatever answers DF has;
every rule that reads it is guarded by the filing status, as in DF.

## Declarations

```catala-metadata
## The marital status the primary filer tells Direct File. DF:
## filers.xml /maritalStatusOptions. `NeverMarried` is DF `single`.
declaration enumeration MaritalStatus:
  -- NeverMarried
  -- Married
  -- Divorced
  -- Widowed

## When the widowed filer's spouse died. DF: filers.xml /yearOfSpouseDeathOptions.
## Only read when the marital status is `Widowed`; a filer who is not widowed
## is never asked, and the value then does not matter.
declaration enumeration YearOfSpouseDeath:
  -- DiedInTaxYear
  -- DiedTaxYearMinusOne
  -- DiedTaxYearMinusTwo
  -- DiedBeforeTaxYearMinusTwo

## How long the spouses lived together. DF: filers.xml
## /spouseLivedTogetherMonthsOptions. Only read when the spouses did not live
## together all year.
declaration enumeration SpouseLivedTogetherMonths:
  -- LivedApartAllYear
  -- LivedTogetherSixMonthsOrLess
  -- LivedTogetherMoreThanSixMonths

## The `Writable` answers DF keeps per filer (collection `/filers/*`).
## Only the answers that feed tax rules are kept (see the list of omitted
## facts at the top of this file).
declaration structure FilerAnswers:
  # DF: /filers/*/dateOfBirth
  data date_of_birth content date
  # DF: /filers/*/isBlind
  data is_blind content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/canBeClaimed
  data can_be_claimed content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/willBeClaimed
  data will_be_claimed content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/potentialClaimerMustFile
  data potential_claimer_must_file content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/potentialClaimerDidFile
  data potential_claimer_did_file content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/isUsCitizenFullYear
  data is_us_citizen_full_year content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/writableCitizenAtEndOfTaxYear
  data writable_citizen_at_end_of_tax_year content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/writableIsNoncitizenResidentFullYear
  data writable_is_noncitizen_resident_full_year content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/writableIsNational
  data writable_is_national content boolean

## The tax year. DF: constants.xml /taxYear (`<Int>2024</Int>`).
declaration tax_year content integer equals 2024

## Ages used by the rules below, all fixed by statute or by a DF product
## decision (none is inflation indexed).
## IRC 63(f)(1): "attained age 65". IRC 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(II): "age 25 but not
## attained age 65". DF /filers/*/age55OrOlder (age 55, Form 8880 / retirement
## helpers) and /filers/*/isUnder18 (Saver's Credit, IRC 25B(c)(2)(C)).
declaration senior_age content integer equals 65
declaration eitc_minimum_age content integer equals 25
declaration eitc_maximum_age content integer equals 64
declaration age_55 content integer equals 55
declaration adult_age content integer equals 18
## DF product decision: filers.xml /flowKnockoutFilerAgeYoungerThan16. There is
## no statute for the number 16; Direct File does not serve filers under 16.
declaration minimum_supported_filer_age content integer equals 16

## Completed years from `start_date` to `end_date` (the later one): the year
## difference, less one if `end_date` falls before the anniversary of
## `start_date` in its year. Used for the age of a spouse who died during the
## year. DF writes the same comparison out by month and day
## (filers.xml /secondaryFilerAgeDayBeforeDeath, line 3457).
declaration completed_years content integer
  depends on start_date content date, end_date content date equals
  (Date.get_year of end_date - Date.get_year of start_date) -
  (if (Date.get_month of end_date < Date.get_month of start_date)
      or (Date.get_month of end_date = Date.get_month of start_date
          and Date.get_day of end_date < Date.get_day of start_date)
   then 1 else 0)
```

## Age of one filer

### Age 65 and the day before the birthday

Pub. 501 (2024), `sources/pubs/p501--2024.pdf` p 3: "A person is considered to
reach age 65 on the day before the person's 65th birthday." For a filer born
on January 1, 1960, that is December 31, 2024, so the filer is 65 at the end of
2024; for a filer born on January 2, 1960, it is January 1, 2025, so they are
not. DF counts the birthday as the day before the date of birth
(`/filers/*/dayBeforeDateOfBirth`, line 357) and subtracts years only:
`/filers/*/ageCalculatedDayBeforeDOB` = tax year minus the year of that day
(line 371), and `/filers/*/age` = tax year minus the year of birth (line 411).
Both are the age on December 31 of the tax year.

### Age for the Earned Income Credit without a qualifying child

IRC 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(II): "such individual (or, if the individual is married,
either the individual or the individual's spouse) has attained age 25 but not
attained age 65 before the close of the taxable year". Pub. 596 (2024),
`sources/pubs/p596--2024.pdf` p 16, Rule 11: "You meet the age test if you were
born after December 31, 1959, and before January 2, 2000." and "Your spouse is
considered to reach age 25 on the day before their 25th birthday. However, the
rule for reaching age 65 is different; your spouse reaches age 65 on their 65th
birthday." The minimum age (25) therefore uses the day before the birthday
and the maximum age (64 or younger) uses the actual birthday. DF
`/filers/*/ageForSelfOnlyEitcLimits` (line 786) implements this: the day-before
age if that age is 25, otherwise the plain age.

For a spouse who died in the tax year, Pub. 596 p 16: "A taxpayer who died in
2024 meets the age test if the taxpayer was at least age 25 but under age 65 at
the time of death." The 25 is reached on the day before the 25th birthday
(`/secondaryFilerAgeDayBeforeDeath`, line 3457) and the 65 on the 65th birthday
(`/secondaryFilerAgeDayOfDeath`, line 3558).

For the standard deduction, Pub. 501 p 3: "Even if the taxpayer was born before
January 2, 1960, the taxpayer isn't considered 65 or older at the end of 2024
unless the taxpayer was 65 or older at the time of death." That is the age at
death, with the day before the birthday: `/MFJDeceasedSpouseReachedAge65ForStandardD`
(line 3659).

```catala-metadata
declaration scope FilerFacts:
  # DF: /filers/*/dateOfBirth
  input date_of_birth content date
  # True for the secondary filer when the spouse died in the tax year
  # (DF: /isWidowedInTaxYear and /filers/*/isSecondaryFiler).
  input is_deceased_in_tax_year condition
  # DF: /secondaryFilerDateOfDeath. Read only if `is_deceased_in_tax_year`.
  input date_of_death content date
  # DF: /filers/*/isUsCitizenFullYear
  input is_us_citizen_full_year condition
  # DF: /filers/*/writableCitizenAtEndOfTaxYear
  input writable_citizen_at_end_of_tax_year condition
  # DF: /filers/*/writableIsNoncitizenResidentFullYear
  input writable_is_noncitizen_resident_full_year condition
  # DF: /filers/*/writableIsNational
  input writable_is_national condition

  # DF: /filers/*/dayBeforeDateOfBirth
  internal day_before_date_of_birth content date
  # DF: /filers/*/age
  output age content integer
  # DF: /filers/*/ageCalculatedDayBeforeDOB
  output age_calculated_day_before_dob content integer
  # DF: /filers/*/age65OrOlder
  output age65_or_older condition
  # DF: /filers/*/age55OrOlder
  output age55_or_older condition
  # DF: /filers/*/youngerThan16
  output younger_than16 condition
  # DF: /filers/*/isUnder18
  output is_under18 condition
  # DF: /secondaryFilerAgeDayBeforeDeath (meaningful only if deceased)
  internal age_day_before_death content integer
  # DF: /secondaryFilerAgeDayOfDeath (meaningful only if deceased)
  internal age_day_of_death content integer
  # DF: /MFJDeceasedSpouseReachedAge65ForStandardD (false if not deceased)
  output reached_age65_at_death condition
  # DF: /filers/*/ageForSelfOnlyEitcLimits
  output age_for_self_only_eitc_limits content integer
  # DF: /filers/*/age25OrOlderForEitc
  output age25_or_older_for_eitc condition
  # DF: /filers/*/age64OrYoungerForEitc
  output age64_or_younger_for_eitc condition

  # DF: /filers/*/citizenAtEndOfTaxYear
  output citizen_at_end_of_tax_year condition
  # DF: /filers/*/isNoncitizenResidentFullYear
  output is_noncitizen_resident_full_year condition
  # DF: /filers/*/isNational
  output is_national condition
  # DF: /filers/*/isCitizenOrNational
  output is_citizen_or_national condition
  # DF: /primaryFilerIsCitizenOrRAAllYear, /secondaryFilerIsCitizenOrRAAllYear
  output is_citizen_or_ra_all_year condition
  # DF: /primaryFilerIsCitizenOrNational, /secondaryFilerIsCitizenOrNational
  output is_citizen_or_national_for_return condition
```

```catala
scope FilerFacts:
  # DF: /filers/*/dayBeforeDateOfBirth
  definition day_before_date_of_birth equals date_of_birth - 1 day

  # DF: /filers/*/age = taxYear - year(dateOfBirth)
  definition age equals tax_year - Date.get_year of date_of_birth

  # DF: /filers/*/ageCalculatedDayBeforeDOB = taxYear - year(dayBeforeDateOfBirth)
  definition age_calculated_day_before_dob equals
    tax_year - Date.get_year of day_before_date_of_birth

  # IRC 63(f)(1)(A); Pub 501 p 3. DF: /filers/*/age65OrOlder
  definition age65_or_older equals age_calculated_day_before_dob >= senior_age

  # DF: /filers/*/age55OrOlder
  definition age55_or_older equals age >= age_55

  # DF: /filers/*/youngerThan16
  definition younger_than16 equals age < minimum_supported_filer_age

  # DF: /filers/*/isUnder18 (day-before-birthday age, IRC 25B(c)(2)(C))
  definition is_under18 equals age_calculated_day_before_dob < adult_age

  # Pub 596 p 16. DF: /secondaryFilerAgeDayBeforeDeath
  definition age_day_before_death equals
    completed_years of day_before_date_of_birth, date_of_death

  # Pub 596 p 16. DF: /secondaryFilerAgeDayOfDeath
  definition age_day_of_death equals completed_years of date_of_birth, date_of_death

  # Pub 501 p 3. DF: /MFJDeceasedSpouseReachedAge65ForStandardD
  definition reached_age65_at_death equals
    is_deceased_in_tax_year and age_day_before_death >= senior_age

  # Pub 596 p 16. DF: /filers/*/ageForSelfOnlyEitcLimits, case by case in
  # the order of the DF switch.
  definition age_for_self_only_eitc_limits equals
    if is_deceased_in_tax_year and age = eitc_minimum_age
    then age_day_before_death
    else if is_deceased_in_tax_year
    then age_day_of_death
    else if age_calculated_day_before_dob = eitc_minimum_age
    then age_calculated_day_before_dob
    else age

  # IRC 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(II). DF: /filers/*/age25OrOlderForEitc
  definition age25_or_older_for_eitc equals
    age_for_self_only_eitc_limits >= eitc_minimum_age

  # IRC 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(II). DF: /filers/*/age64OrYoungerForEitc
  definition age64_or_younger_for_eitc equals
    age_for_self_only_eitc_limits <= eitc_maximum_age

  # DF: /filers/*/citizenAtEndOfTaxYear
  definition citizen_at_end_of_tax_year equals
    (not is_us_citizen_full_year) and writable_citizen_at_end_of_tax_year

  # DF: /filers/*/isNoncitizenResidentFullYear
  definition is_noncitizen_resident_full_year equals
    (not is_us_citizen_full_year) and (not citizen_at_end_of_tax_year)
    and writable_is_noncitizen_resident_full_year

  # DF: /filers/*/isNational
  definition is_national equals
    (not is_us_citizen_full_year) and (not citizen_at_end_of_tax_year)
    and is_noncitizen_resident_full_year and writable_is_national

  # DF: /filers/*/isCitizenOrNational
  definition is_citizen_or_national equals
    is_us_citizen_full_year or is_noncitizen_resident_full_year or is_national

  # DF: /primaryFilerIsCitizenOrRAAllYear
  definition is_citizen_or_ra_all_year equals
    is_noncitizen_resident_full_year or is_us_citizen_full_year
    or citizen_at_end_of_tax_year

  # DF: /primaryFilerIsCitizenOrNational
  definition is_citizen_or_national_for_return equals
    is_us_citizen_full_year or citizen_at_end_of_tax_year or is_national
```

## The filers of the return

### Marital status

IRC 7703(a): "(1) the determination of whether an individual is married shall
be made as of the close of his taxable year; except that if his spouse dies
during his taxable year such determination shall be made as of the time of such
death; and (2) an individual legally separated from his spouse under a decree
of divorce or of separate maintenance shall not be considered as married."
(`sources/statute/irc-7703.html`.) DF asks the primary filer for the marital
status (`/maritalStatus`, line 4196) and, for a widowed filer, the year of the
death (`/yearOfSpouseDeath`, line 4464). A filer who is married or was widowed
in the tax year may file as married (`filingStatus.xml` `/maritalStatusAllowsFilingMarried`).

### Joint returns and the spouse's residency

IRC 6013(a)(1): "no joint return shall be made if either the husband or wife at
any time during the taxable year is a nonresident alien". IRC 6013(g)(1)-(2)
lets a nonresident alien married to a citizen or resident elect to be treated
as a resident. DF `/secondaryFilerResidencyEligibleForMFJ` (line 3881): the
spouse was a citizen all year, a citizen at the end of the year (having started
the year as a resident), or a noncitizen resident the whole year (which
includes the 6013(g) election).

### Lived apart

IRC 7703(b)(3): "during the last 6 months of the taxable year, such
individual's spouse is not a member of such household, such individual shall
not be considered as married." Direct File derives the answer from three
questions (`/livedTogetherAllYearWithSpouse`, `/spouseLivedTogetherMonths`,
`/writableLivedApartLastSixMonths`, lines 3963 to 4102). The child and
support tests of 7703(b)(1)-(2) are in the household modules (#19), not here.

### Claimed as a dependent

IRC 63(c)(5) and Pub. 501 p 3 limit the standard deduction of "an individual
with respect to whom a deduction under section 151 is allowable to another
taxpayer". Direct File does not decide that from a second return (quirk Q6 in
CONVENTIONS section 8): it asks whether someone can claim the filer
(`canBeClaimed`), whether they expect to be claimed (`willBeClaimed`) and
whether the person who could claim them must file or filed for more than a
refund (`potentialClaimerMustFile`, `potentialClaimerDidFile`,
`primaryFilerPotentialClaimerFiledOnlyForRefund`).
`/treatFilersAsDependents` (line 1441) is true when the filers are treated as
dependents: they then get the reduced standard deduction and cannot claim
dependents, CTC or ODC. For a joint return the couple is treated as
dependents only if one spouse can be claimed, the couple is not required to
file, and they chose to file for a refund only (`/isMFJDependent`, line 1510).

Direct File's `Placeholder` for `/taxpayerCannotBeClaimed` (false) is the
engine default for an incomplete input and is not modelled (inputs are complete).

### Knockouts

scope.md section 9 item 1, and `flow.xml` lines 14 to 20 (`/flowIsKnockedOut`).
The six knockouts of `filers.xml` are: filer under 16, spouse itemizes,
primary-filer residency, unsupported state, registered domestic partnership,
community property. The state one (`/flowKnockoutUnsupportedState`) belongs to
the state-scoping issue and is not modelled here (listed at the top of this
file). The other five are `ko_` conditions below.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Filers:
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /filingStatus (Writable)
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # DF: /maritalStatus
  input marital_status content MaritalStatus
  # DF: /yearOfSpouseDeath
  input year_of_spouse_death content YearOfSpouseDeath
  # DF: /primaryFiler/* (the filer with isPrimaryFiler)
  input primary_filer content FilerAnswers
  # DF: /secondaryFiler/*
  input secondary_filer content FilerAnswers
  # DF: /secondaryFilerDateOfDeath. Read only if the spouse died in the tax year.
  input secondary_filer_date_of_death content date
  # DF: /primaryFilerPotentialClaimerFiledOnlyForRefund
  input primary_filer_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund condition
  # DF: /MFJRequiredToFile
  input mfj_required_to_file condition
  # DF: /MFJDependentsFilingForCredits
  input mfj_dependents_filing_for_credits condition
  # DF: /livedTogetherAllYearWithSpouse
  input lived_together_all_year_with_spouse condition
  # DF: /spouseLivedTogetherMonths
  input spouse_lived_together_months content SpouseLivedTogetherMonths
  # DF: /writableLivedApartLastSixMonths
  input writable_lived_apart_last_six_months condition
  # DF: /writableSeparationAgreement
  input writable_separation_agreement condition
  # DF: /canFileJointlyYearOfSpouseDeath
  input can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death condition
  # DF: /inRegisteredDomesticPartnership
  input in_registered_domestic_partnership condition
  # DF: /filerResidenceAndIncomeState
  input filer_residence_and_income_state content Types.ScopedState
  # DF: /spouseItemizes
  input spouse_itemizes condition
  # DF: /MFSLivingSpouseFilingReturn
  input mfs_living_spouse_filing_return condition
  # DF: /MFSDeceasedSpouseFilingReturn
  input mfs_deceased_spouse_filing_return condition
  # DF: /MFSSpouseHasGrossIncome
  input mfs_spouse_has_gross_income condition
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /eligibleForHoh. Computed by the household and
  # filing-status modules (#19, #20), which run after this one (CONVENTIONS
  # section 7, stage 3); only the community-property knockout reads it here.
  input eligible_for_hoh condition

  primary_facts scope FilerFacts
  secondary_facts scope FilerFacts

  # Marital status
  # DF: /isMarried
  output is_married condition
  # DF: /isSingle
  output is_single condition
  # DF: /isWidowed
  output is_widowed condition
  # DF: /isWidowedInTaxYear
  output is_widowed_in_tax_year condition
  # DF: /widowedBeforeTaxYearMinusTwo
  output widowed_before_tax_year_minus_two condition
  # DF: /widowedCouldQualifyForQSS
  output widowed_could_qualify_for_qss condition
  # DF: /filerCouldQualifyForQss
  output filer_could_qualify_for_qss condition

  # Filing status basics (DF: filingStatus.xml; CONVENTIONS section 7, stage 1)
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /isFilingStatusMFJ
  output is_filing_status_mfj condition
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /maritalStatusAllowsFilingMarried
  internal marital_status_allows_filing_married condition
  # DF: /secondaryFilerResidencyEligibleForMFJ
  output secondary_filer_residency_eligible_for_mfj condition
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /eligibleForMFJ
  output eligible_for_mfj condition
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /eligibleForMFS
  output eligible_for_mfs condition
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /eligibleForSingle
  output eligible_for_single condition
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsMFJ
  output treat_as_mfj condition
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsMFS
  output treat_as_mfs condition
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsHoh
  internal treat_as_hoh condition

  # Lived apart
  # DF: /livedTogetherSixMonthsOrLess
  internal lived_together_six_months_or_less condition
  # DF: /livedTogetherMoreThanSixMonths
  internal lived_together_more_than_six_months condition
  # DF: /livedApartAllYear
  output lived_apart_all_year condition
  # DF: /livedApartLastSixMonths
  output lived_apart_last_six_months condition
  # DF: /separationAgreement
  output separation_agreement condition
  # DF: /specialRuleForSeparatedSpouses
  output special_rule_for_separated_spouses condition
  # DF: /filerCouldQualifyForHoh
  output filer_could_qualify_for_hoh condition
  # DF: /mfsFilerCouldBeConsiderUnmarriedForCdcc
  output mfs_filer_could_be_considered_unmarried_for_cdcc condition
  # DF: /filersCouldQualifyForCdcc
  output filers_could_qualify_for_cdcc condition

  # Ages of both filers
  # DF: /primaryFiler/age
  output primary_filer_age content integer
  # DF: /secondaryFiler/age
  output secondary_filer_age content integer
  # DF: /primaryFiler/age65OrOlder
  output primary_filer_age65_or_older condition
  # DF: /secondaryFiler/age65OrOlder
  output secondary_filer_age65_or_older condition
  # DF: /primaryFiler/age25OrOlderForEitc
  output primary_filer_age25_or_older_for_eitc condition
  # DF: /secondaryFiler/age25OrOlderForEitc
  output secondary_filer_age25_or_older_for_eitc condition
  # DF: /primaryFiler/age64OrYoungerForEitc
  output primary_filer_age64_or_younger_for_eitc condition
  # DF: /secondaryFiler/age64OrYoungerForEitc
  output secondary_filer_age64_or_younger_for_eitc condition
  # DF: /MFJDeceasedSpouseReachedAge65ForStandardD
  output mfj_deceased_spouse_reached_age65_for_standard_d condition
  # DF: /atLeastOneTpIs65OrOlder
  output at_least_one_tp_is_65_or_older condition
  # DF: /atLeastOneTpIsUnder65
  output at_least_one_tp_is_under_65 condition
  # DF: /xmlOver65SRIndicator (1040-SR)
  output xml_over65_sr_indicator condition
  # DF: /minimumFilerDateOfBirth (date of birth of the oldest filer)
  output minimum_filer_date_of_birth content date

  # Citizenship and residency
  # DF: /filersUSCitizenOrRAAllYear
  output filers_us_citizen_or_ra_all_year condition
  # DF: /eitherFilerUSCitizenOrNational
  output either_filer_us_citizen_or_national condition
  # DF: /allEligibleFilersAreUSCitizensOrNationals
  output all_eligible_filers_are_us_citizens_or_nationals condition
  # DF: /isSecondaryFilerNra
  output is_secondary_filer_nra condition

  # Claimed as a dependent
  # DF: /primaryFilerCouldBeDependentAndClaimerIsRequiredToFileOrFilingForCredits
  output primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits condition
  # DF: /notMfjAndPrimaryFilerCouldBeDependentAndClaimerIsRequiredToFileOrFilingForCredits
  output not_mfj_and_primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits condition
  # DF: /eitherFilerCanBeClaimed
  output either_filer_can_be_claimed condition
  # DF: /MFJClaimingRefundOnly
  output mfj_claiming_refund_only condition
  # DF: /MFJNotRequiredToFileAndEitherFilerCanBeClaimed
  output mfj_not_required_to_file_and_either_filer_can_be_claimed condition
  # DF: /flowMFJSpouseFilingRequirementSubsection
  internal flow_mfj_spouse_filing_requirement_subsection condition
  # DF: /isMFJDependent
  output is_mfj_dependent condition
  # DF: /taxpayerCannotBeClaimed
  output taxpayer_cannot_be_claimed condition
  # DF: /primaryFilerIsClaimedAsDependent
  output primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent condition
  # DF: /secondaryFilerIsClaimedAsDependent
  output secondary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent condition
  # DF: /eitherFilerIsClaimedAsDependent
  output either_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent condition
  # DF: /treatFilersAsDependents
  output treat_filers_as_dependents condition
  # DF: /filersCouldntBeDependents
  output filers_couldnt_be_dependents condition
  # DF: /primarySomeoneCanClaimForTaxBenefits (Form 1040 dependent checkbox)
  output primary_some_one_can_claim_for_tax_benefits condition
  # DF: /secondarySomeoneCanClaimForTaxBenefits
  output secondary_some_one_can_claim_for_tax_benefits condition
  # DF: /isSpouseExempt
  output is_spouse_exempt condition

  # MFS spouse (standard deduction inputs)
  # DF: /MFSSpouseFilingReturnDerived
  internal mfs_spouse_filing_return_derived condition
  # DF: /MFSSpouseProvidesNoBenefits
  output mfs_spouse_provides_no_benefits condition

  # Knockouts (CONVENTIONS section 6)
  # DF: /livesInCommunityPropertyState
  internal lives_in_community_property_state condition
  # DF: /checkForRegisteredDomesticPartner
  internal check_for_registered_domestic_partner condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutFilerAgeYoungerThan16
  output ko_flow_knockout_filer_age_younger_than16 condition
  # DF: /spouseItemizesKnockout
  output ko_spouse_itemizes_knockout condition
  # DF: /primaryFilerResidencyKnockout
  output ko_primary_filer_residency_knockout condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHasApplicableRegisteredDomesticPartnership
  output ko_flow_knockout_has_applicable_registered_domestic_partnership condition
  # DF: /knockoutSubjectToCommunityPropertyLaws
  output ko_knockout_subject_to_community_property_laws condition
  # The knockouts of this module, listed in one place (CONVENTIONS section 6).
  output unsupported condition
```

### Sub-scope wiring

```catala
scope Filers:
  definition primary_facts.date_of_birth equals primary_filer.date_of_birth
  definition primary_facts.is_deceased_in_tax_year equals false
  definition primary_facts.date_of_death equals secondary_filer_date_of_death
  definition primary_facts.is_us_citizen_full_year equals
    primary_filer.is_us_citizen_full_year
  definition primary_facts.writable_citizen_at_end_of_tax_year equals
    primary_filer.writable_citizen_at_end_of_tax_year
  definition primary_facts.writable_is_noncitizen_resident_full_year equals
    primary_filer.writable_is_noncitizen_resident_full_year
  definition primary_facts.writable_is_national equals
    primary_filer.writable_is_national

  definition secondary_facts.date_of_birth equals secondary_filer.date_of_birth
  definition secondary_facts.is_deceased_in_tax_year equals is_widowed_in_tax_year
  definition secondary_facts.date_of_death equals secondary_filer_date_of_death
  definition secondary_facts.is_us_citizen_full_year equals
    secondary_filer.is_us_citizen_full_year
  definition secondary_facts.writable_citizen_at_end_of_tax_year equals
    secondary_filer.writable_citizen_at_end_of_tax_year
  definition secondary_facts.writable_is_noncitizen_resident_full_year equals
    secondary_filer.writable_is_noncitizen_resident_full_year
  definition secondary_facts.writable_is_national equals
    secondary_filer.writable_is_national

  definition primary_filer_age equals primary_facts.age
  definition secondary_filer_age equals secondary_facts.age
  definition primary_filer_age65_or_older equals primary_facts.age65_or_older
  definition secondary_filer_age65_or_older equals secondary_facts.age65_or_older
  definition primary_filer_age25_or_older_for_eitc equals
    primary_facts.age25_or_older_for_eitc
  definition secondary_filer_age25_or_older_for_eitc equals
    secondary_facts.age25_or_older_for_eitc
  definition primary_filer_age64_or_younger_for_eitc equals
    primary_facts.age64_or_younger_for_eitc
  definition secondary_filer_age64_or_younger_for_eitc equals
    secondary_facts.age64_or_younger_for_eitc
  definition mfj_deceased_spouse_reached_age65_for_standard_d equals
    secondary_facts.reached_age65_at_death
```

### Marital status rules

```catala
scope Filers:
  # DF: /isMarried
  definition is_married equals marital_status = Married
  # DF: /isSingle
  definition is_single equals marital_status = NeverMarried
  # DF: /isWidowed
  definition is_widowed equals marital_status = Widowed

  # IRC 7703(a)(1). DF: /isWidowedInTaxYear
  definition is_widowed_in_tax_year equals
    is_widowed and year_of_spouse_death = DiedInTaxYear

  # DF: /widowedBeforeTaxYearMinusTwo
  definition widowed_before_tax_year_minus_two equals
    is_widowed and year_of_spouse_death = DiedBeforeTaxYearMinusTwo

  # IRC 2(a): a surviving spouse is a widow(er) in the two years after the death.
  # DF: /widowedCouldQualifyForQSS
  definition widowed_could_qualify_for_qss equals
    is_widowed and (year_of_spouse_death = DiedTaxYearMinusOne
                    or year_of_spouse_death = DiedTaxYearMinusTwo)

  # DF: /filerCouldQualifyForQss
  definition filer_could_qualify_for_qss equals
    widowed_could_qualify_for_qss and can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death
```

### Filing status basics

Stage 1 of CONVENTIONS section 7. `eligible_for_mfj` reads only marital and
residency facts, so it is computed here; the household-dependent
`eligible_for_hoh`, `eligible_for_qss` and the final check are stage 3 (#20).

```catala
scope Filers:
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /isFilingStatusMFJ
  definition is_filing_status_mfj equals filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly

  # IRC 7703(a). DF: filingStatus.xml /maritalStatusAllowsFilingMarried
  definition marital_status_allows_filing_married equals
    is_married or is_widowed_in_tax_year

  # IRC 6013(a)(1), (g). DF: /secondaryFilerResidencyEligibleForMFJ
  definition secondary_filer_residency_eligible_for_mfj equals
    secondary_filer.is_us_citizen_full_year
    or secondary_facts.citizen_at_end_of_tax_year
    or secondary_facts.is_noncitizen_resident_full_year

  # DF: filingStatus.xml /eligibleForMFJ
  definition eligible_for_mfj equals
    marital_status_allows_filing_married
    and secondary_filer_residency_eligible_for_mfj

  # DF: filingStatus.xml /eligibleForMFS
  definition eligible_for_mfs equals marital_status_allows_filing_married

  # DF: filingStatus.xml /eligibleForSingle
  definition eligible_for_single equals not marital_status_allows_filing_married

  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsMFJ (the filing status is complete, so only
  # the first branch of the DF `Any` applies)
  definition treat_as_mfj equals is_filing_status_mfj and eligible_for_mfj

  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsMFS
  definition treat_as_mfs equals filing_status = MarriedFilingSeparately

  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsHoh
  definition treat_as_hoh equals filing_status = HeadOfHousehold
```

### Lived apart rules

```catala
scope Filers:
  # DF: /livedTogetherSixMonthsOrLess
  definition lived_together_six_months_or_less equals
    (not lived_together_all_year_with_spouse)
    and spouse_lived_together_months = LivedTogetherSixMonthsOrLess

  # DF: /livedTogetherMoreThanSixMonths
  definition lived_together_more_than_six_months equals
    (not lived_together_all_year_with_spouse)
    and spouse_lived_together_months = LivedTogetherMoreThanSixMonths

  # DF: /livedApartAllYear
  definition lived_apart_all_year equals
    (not lived_together_all_year_with_spouse)
    and spouse_lived_together_months = LivedApartAllYear

  # IRC 7703(b)(3). DF: /livedApartLastSixMonths (the DF switch in order; the
  # three cases cover every complete input, the last `else` is never reached)
  definition lived_apart_last_six_months equals
    if lived_together_more_than_six_months or lived_together_all_year_with_spouse
    then false
    else if lived_apart_all_year then true
    else if lived_together_six_months_or_less
    then writable_lived_apart_last_six_months
    else false

  # DF: /separationAgreement
  definition separation_agreement equals
    if lived_together_all_year_with_spouse then false
    else writable_separation_agreement

  # DF: /specialRuleForSeparatedSpouses
  definition special_rule_for_separated_spouses equals
    lived_apart_last_six_months or separation_agreement

  # DF: /filerCouldQualifyForHoh. Uses eligible_for_mfj, not eligible_for_hoh
  # (CONVENTIONS section 7, stage 1).
  definition filer_could_qualify_for_hoh equals
    (not eligible_for_mfj) or (eligible_for_mfj and lived_apart_last_six_months)

  # Form 2441 instructions: an MFS filer is considered unmarried if they
  # "lived apart from your spouse during the last 6 months". The per-qualifying-person
  # requirements are in #28. DF: /mfsFilerCouldBeConsiderUnmarriedForCdcc
  definition mfs_filer_could_be_considered_unmarried_for_cdcc equals
    treat_as_mfs and lived_apart_last_six_months

  # DF: /filersCouldQualifyForCdcc
  definition filers_could_qualify_for_cdcc equals
    if treat_as_mfs then mfs_filer_could_be_considered_unmarried_for_cdcc
    else true
```

### Ages of both filers

```catala
scope Filers:
  # DF: /atLeastOneTpIs65OrOlder
  definition at_least_one_tp_is_65_or_older equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj
    then primary_filer_age65_or_older or secondary_filer_age65_or_older
    else primary_filer_age65_or_older

  # DF: /atLeastOneTpIsUnder65
  definition at_least_one_tp_is_under_65 equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj
    then (not primary_filer_age65_or_older) or (not secondary_filer_age65_or_older)
    else not primary_filer_age65_or_older

  # DF: /xmlOver65SRIndicator
  definition xml_over65_sr_indicator equals
    primary_filer_age65_or_older
    or (is_filing_status_mfj and secondary_filer_age65_or_older)

  # "for purposes of the age test for qualifying children" (IRC 152(c)(3)).
  # DF: /minimumFilerDateOfBirth. The secondary date of birth is complete
  # whenever the return is joint.
  definition minimum_filer_date_of_birth equals
    if treat_as_mfj and secondary_filer.date_of_birth < primary_filer.date_of_birth
    then secondary_filer.date_of_birth
    else primary_filer.date_of_birth
```

### Citizenship and residency rules

```catala
scope Filers:
  # DF: /filersUSCitizenOrRAAllYear
  definition filers_us_citizen_or_ra_all_year equals
    if treat_as_mfj
    then primary_facts.is_citizen_or_ra_all_year and secondary_facts.is_citizen_or_ra_all_year
    else primary_facts.is_citizen_or_ra_all_year

  # DF: /eitherFilerUSCitizenOrNational
  definition either_filer_us_citizen_or_national equals
    if treat_as_mfj
    then primary_facts.is_citizen_or_national_for_return
         or secondary_facts.is_citizen_or_national_for_return
    else primary_facts.is_citizen_or_national_for_return

  # DF: /allEligibleFilersAreUSCitizensOrNationals
  definition all_eligible_filers_are_us_citizens_or_nationals equals
    if treat_as_mfj
    then primary_facts.is_citizen_or_national_for_return
         and secondary_facts.is_citizen_or_national_for_return
    else primary_facts.is_citizen_or_national_for_return

  # DF: /isSecondaryFilerNra
  definition is_secondary_filer_nra equals not secondary_facts.is_citizen_or_ra_all_year
```

### Dependency rules

```catala
scope Filers:
  # DF: /primaryFilerCouldBeDependentAndClaimerIsRequiredToFileOrFilingForCredits
  definition primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits equals
    primary_filer.can_be_claimed
    and (primary_filer.potential_claimer_must_file
         or ((not primary_filer.potential_claimer_must_file)
             and primary_filer.potential_claimer_did_file
             and not primary_filer_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund))

  # DF: /notMfjAndPrimaryFilerCouldBeDependent...
  definition not_mfj_and_primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits equals
    (not is_filing_status_mfj)
    and primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits

  # DF: /eitherFilerCanBeClaimed
  definition either_filer_can_be_claimed equals
    primary_filer.can_be_claimed or secondary_filer.can_be_claimed

  # DF: /MFJClaimingRefundOnly
  definition mfj_claiming_refund_only equals not mfj_dependents_filing_for_credits

  # DF: /MFJNotRequiredToFileAndEitherFilerCanBeClaimed
  definition mfj_not_required_to_file_and_either_filer_can_be_claimed equals
    (not mfj_required_to_file) and either_filer_can_be_claimed

  # DF: /flowMFJSpouseFilingRequirementSubsection
  definition flow_mfj_spouse_filing_requirement_subsection equals
    secondary_filer.can_be_claimed
    or ((not secondary_filer.can_be_claimed)
        and primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits)

  # Pub 501 (2024) p 3, joint return test for dependents. DF: /isMFJDependent
  definition is_mfj_dependent equals
    treat_as_mfj
    and flow_mfj_spouse_filing_requirement_subsection
    and (not mfj_required_to_file)
    and mfj_claiming_refund_only

  # DF: /taxpayerCannotBeClaimed
  definition taxpayer_cannot_be_claimed equals
    treat_as_mfj
    and flow_mfj_spouse_filing_requirement_subsection
    and (not mfj_required_to_file)
    and (not mfj_claiming_refund_only)

  # DF: /primaryFilerIsClaimedAsDependent
  definition primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent equals
    primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits
    and primary_filer.will_be_claimed
    and not taxpayer_cannot_be_claimed

  # DF: /secondaryFilerIsClaimedAsDependent
  definition secondary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent equals
    treat_as_mfj
    and (not mfj_required_to_file)
    and secondary_filer.can_be_claimed
    and secondary_filer.will_be_claimed
    and not taxpayer_cannot_be_claimed

  # DF: /eitherFilerIsClaimedAsDependent
  definition either_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent equals
    primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent or secondary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent

  # IRC 63(c)(5); Pub 501 p 3. DF: /treatFilersAsDependents. The filing
  # status is complete, so /isMFJDependent is complete too.
  definition treat_filers_as_dependents equals
    if treat_as_mfj then is_mfj_dependent
    else primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits

  # DF: /filersCouldntBeDependents
  definition filers_couldnt_be_dependents equals
    if treat_as_mfj then not is_mfj_dependent
    else not primary_filer.can_be_claimed

  # DF: /primarySomeoneCanClaimForTaxBenefits
  definition primary_some_one_can_claim_for_tax_benefits equals
    (is_filing_status_mfj and is_mfj_dependent
     and primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits)
    or not_mfj_and_primary_filer_could_be_dependent_and_claimer_is_required_to_file_or_filing_for_credits

  # DF: /secondarySomeoneCanClaimForTaxBenefits
  definition secondary_some_one_can_claim_for_tax_benefits equals
    is_filing_status_mfj and is_mfj_dependent and secondary_filer.can_be_claimed

  # DF: /isSpouseExempt
  definition is_spouse_exempt equals
    (not secondary_filer.can_be_claimed) and is_filing_status_mfj
```

### MFS spouse

Pub. 501 (2024): a married person filing separately may claim the spouse's
additional standard deduction only if the spouse has no gross income, is not
filing a return and cannot be claimed as a dependent. DF encodes the negation
as `/MFSSpouseProvidesNoBenefits` (line 3837).

```catala
scope Filers:
  # DF: /MFSSpouseFilingReturnDerived. A widowed filer is asked about a
  # return filed for the deceased spouse, anyone else about the living spouse.
  definition mfs_spouse_filing_return_derived equals
    if is_widowed then mfs_deceased_spouse_filing_return
    else mfs_living_spouse_filing_return

  # DF: /MFSSpouseProvidesNoBenefits
  definition mfs_spouse_provides_no_benefits equals
    mfs_spouse_filing_return_derived
    or mfs_spouse_has_gross_income
    or secondary_filer.can_be_claimed
```

### Knockout rules

```catala
scope Filers:
  # DF: /livesInCommunityPropertyState. Arizona, California, Idaho, Nevada,
  # New Mexico, Texas, Washington and Wisconsin. Louisiana is commented out in
  # the DF XML (and is not a scoped state). Tennessee and South Dakota, which
  # have elective community property, are excluded as the DF description says.
  definition lives_in_community_property_state equals
    filer_residence_and_income_state = AZ
    or filer_residence_and_income_state = CA
    or filer_residence_and_income_state = ID
    or filer_residence_and_income_state = NM
    or filer_residence_and_income_state = NV
    or filer_residence_and_income_state = TX
    or filer_residence_and_income_state = WA
    or filer_residence_and_income_state = WI

  # DF: /checkForRegisteredDomesticPartner
  definition check_for_registered_domestic_partner equals
    lives_in_community_property_state
    and (marital_status = NeverMarried or marital_status = Divorced
         or marital_status = Widowed)

  # DF: /flowKnockoutFilerAgeYoungerThan16. A young secondary filer only
  # matters for a joint return; Direct File does not offer such a couple MFS.
  rule ko_flow_knockout_filer_age_younger_than16
    under condition
      primary_facts.younger_than16
      or (secondary_facts.younger_than16 and treat_as_mfj)
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /spouseItemizesKnockout
  rule ko_spouse_itemizes_knockout
    under condition spouse_itemizes and mfs_spouse_filing_return_derived
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /primaryFilerResidencyKnockout
  rule ko_primary_filer_residency_knockout
    under condition
      (not primary_filer.is_us_citizen_full_year)
      and (not primary_facts.citizen_at_end_of_tax_year)
      and (not primary_facts.is_noncitizen_resident_full_year)
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /flowKnockoutHasApplicableRegisteredDomesticPartnership
  rule ko_flow_knockout_has_applicable_registered_domestic_partnership
    under condition
      check_for_registered_domestic_partner and in_registered_domestic_partnership
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /knockoutSubjectToCommunityPropertyLaws
  rule ko_knockout_subject_to_community_property_laws
    under condition
      lives_in_community_property_state
      and ((is_married and (not eligible_for_mfj) and (not eligible_for_hoh))
           or treat_as_mfs
           or (treat_as_hoh and marital_status = Married))
    consequence fulfilled

  # The set listed in flow.xml lines 14 to 20 that belongs to this module,
  # except /flowKnockoutUnsupportedState (state scoping, #36).
  rule unsupported
    under condition
      ko_flow_knockout_filer_age_younger_than16
      or ko_spouse_itemizes_knockout
      or ko_primary_filer_residency_knockout
      or ko_flow_knockout_has_applicable_registered_domestic_partnership
      or ko_knockout_subject_to_community_property_laws
    consequence fulfilled
```

## Wiring into the standard deduction

Issue #15: "Wires `age65OrOlder`/dependency flags into the standard-deduction
scope inputs." `FilersStandardDeduction` runs `Filers` and feeds
`Standard_deduction.StandardDeduction` with its outputs. It exists so that the
chain from dates of birth to Form 1040 line 12 is one testable scope (and one
differential test against `/standardDeduction`); the return scope (#14) makes
the same two calls. Only `employer_income_subtotal` (DF income.xml, the earned
income of the dependent minimum) and `mfs_spouse_65_or_older` (a `Writable`
of filers.xml) are added to the inputs of `Filers`.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope FilersStandardDeduction:
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  input marital_status content MaritalStatus
  input year_of_spouse_death content YearOfSpouseDeath
  input primary_filer content FilerAnswers
  input secondary_filer content FilerAnswers
  input secondary_filer_date_of_death content date
  input primary_filer_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund condition
  input mfj_required_to_file condition
  input mfj_dependents_filing_for_credits condition
  input lived_together_all_year_with_spouse condition
  input spouse_lived_together_months content SpouseLivedTogetherMonths
  input writable_lived_apart_last_six_months condition
  input writable_separation_agreement condition
  input can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death condition
  input in_registered_domestic_partnership condition
  input filer_residence_and_income_state content Types.ScopedState
  input spouse_itemizes condition
  input mfs_living_spouse_filing_return condition
  input mfs_deceased_spouse_filing_return condition
  input mfs_spouse_has_gross_income condition
  input eligible_for_hoh condition
  # DF: filers.xml /MFSSpouse65OrOlder (Writable)
  input mfs_spouse_65_or_older condition
  # DF: income.xml /employerIncomeSubtotal
  input employer_income_subtotal content money

  filers scope Filers
  standard_deduction_scope scope SD.StandardDeduction

  # DF: standardDeduction.xml /standardDeduction; Form 1040 line 12
  output standard_deduction content money
  # DF: standardDeduction.xml /additionalStandardDeductionItems
  output additional_standard_deduction_items content integer
  # DF: standardDeduction.xml /isSpouse65OrOlder
  output is_spouse_65_or_older condition
  # DF: filers.xml /secondaryFilerIsBlindIndicatorXml
  output secondary_filer_is_blind_indicator_xml condition
  # DF: filers.xml /xmlOver65SRIndicator, /primarySomeoneCanClaimForTaxBenefits,
  # /secondarySomeoneCanClaimForTaxBenefits (Form 1040 header checkboxes), passed
  # through for the oracle comparison
  output xml_over65_sr_indicator condition
  output primary_some_one_can_claim_for_tax_benefits condition
  output secondary_some_one_can_claim_for_tax_benefits condition
  # Same as filers.unsupported
  output unsupported condition
```

```catala
scope FilersStandardDeduction:
  definition filers.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition filers.marital_status equals marital_status
  definition filers.year_of_spouse_death equals year_of_spouse_death
  definition filers.primary_filer equals primary_filer
  definition filers.secondary_filer equals secondary_filer
  definition filers.secondary_filer_date_of_death equals secondary_filer_date_of_death
  definition filers.primary_filer_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund equals
    primary_filer_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund
  definition filers.mfj_required_to_file equals mfj_required_to_file
  definition filers.mfj_dependents_filing_for_credits equals mfj_dependents_filing_for_credits
  definition filers.lived_together_all_year_with_spouse equals
    lived_together_all_year_with_spouse
  definition filers.spouse_lived_together_months equals spouse_lived_together_months
  definition filers.writable_lived_apart_last_six_months equals
    writable_lived_apart_last_six_months
  definition filers.writable_separation_agreement equals writable_separation_agreement
  definition filers.can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death equals
    can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death
  definition filers.in_registered_domestic_partnership equals
    in_registered_domestic_partnership
  definition filers.filer_residence_and_income_state equals filer_residence_and_income_state
  definition filers.spouse_itemizes equals spouse_itemizes
  definition filers.mfs_living_spouse_filing_return equals mfs_living_spouse_filing_return
  definition filers.mfs_deceased_spouse_filing_return equals
    mfs_deceased_spouse_filing_return
  definition filers.mfs_spouse_has_gross_income equals mfs_spouse_has_gross_income
  definition filers.eligible_for_hoh equals eligible_for_hoh

  definition standard_deduction_scope.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition standard_deduction_scope.treat_as_mfs equals filers.treat_as_mfs
  definition standard_deduction_scope.primary_filer_is_blind equals primary_filer.is_blind
  definition standard_deduction_scope.primary_filer_age65_or_older equals
    filers.primary_filer_age65_or_older
  definition standard_deduction_scope.secondary_filer_is_blind equals
    secondary_filer.is_blind
  definition standard_deduction_scope.secondary_filer_age65_or_older equals
    filers.secondary_filer_age65_or_older
  definition standard_deduction_scope.is_widowed_in_tax_year equals
    filers.is_widowed_in_tax_year
  definition standard_deduction_scope.mfj_deceased_spouse_reached_age65 equals
    filers.mfj_deceased_spouse_reached_age65_for_standard_d
  definition standard_deduction_scope.mfs_spouse_65_or_older equals mfs_spouse_65_or_older
  definition standard_deduction_scope.mfs_spouse_provides_no_benefits equals
    filers.mfs_spouse_provides_no_benefits
  definition standard_deduction_scope.treat_filers_as_dependents equals
    filers.treat_filers_as_dependents
  definition standard_deduction_scope.employer_income_subtotal equals
    employer_income_subtotal

  definition standard_deduction equals standard_deduction_scope.standard_deduction
  definition additional_standard_deduction_items equals
    standard_deduction_scope.additional_standard_deduction_items
  definition is_spouse_65_or_older equals standard_deduction_scope.is_spouse_65_or_older
  definition secondary_filer_is_blind_indicator_xml equals
    standard_deduction_scope.is_spouse_info_applicable_for_standard_deductions
    and secondary_filer.is_blind
  definition xml_over65_sr_indicator equals filers.xml_over65_sr_indicator
  definition primary_some_one_can_claim_for_tax_benefits equals
    filers.primary_some_one_can_claim_for_tax_benefits
  definition secondary_some_one_can_claim_for_tax_benefits equals
    filers.secondary_some_one_can_claim_for_tax_benefits
  definition unsupported equals filers.unsupported
```
